1a:["$","main",null,{"id":"main-content","className":"min-h-screen bg-bg pt-24","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-14","children":[["$","$L21",null,{"href":"/learning-centre","className":"text-sm font-semibold text-accent hover:text-fg transition-colors","children":"Back to Learning Centre"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-8 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8 md:p-10","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent","children":"Budget Leaks · Before You Scale"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-fg md:text-5xl","children":"Fix Landing Page Leaks to Scale Paid Ad Budgets Efficiently"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Raising budget on a page with conversion leaks does not fix the leaks - it scales them. If your current spend is producing a 1% conversion rate, doubling the budget produces twice the traffic at the same 1% rate. The math does not improve until the page does."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-stretch sm:items-center gap-3","children":[["$","$L21",null,{"href":"/audit?utm_source=learning-centre-before-you-raise-ad-budget&utm_medium=hero-cta","className":"inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center justify-center rounded bg-accent px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-bg transition-opacity hover:opacity-85","children":"Get your free audit →"}],["$","$L21",null,{"href":"/repair-sprint","className":"inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center justify-center rounded border border-border px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-fg-muted transition-colors hover:border-fg-muted hover:text-fg","children":"Explore $97 Repair Sprint"}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"The budget multiplier problem"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Ad budget is a multiplier. It amplifies what is already happening on the page - in both directions. If the page converts, more budget produces more customers. If the page leaks, more budget produces more waste at exactly the same rate."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The impulse to raise budget when results are disappointing is understandable - more traffic should produce more signal. But signal from a broken page is noise. You will see more visits, more bounces, and more cost-per-non-conversion. What you will not see is the actual diagnosis, because the traffic is too diluted across a broken experience to isolate which signal is broken."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The correct order is: find and fix the broken signal, verify the page converts on current volume, then scale. Reversing that order accelerates the rate at which you learn nothing useful."}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Is this a page problem or a targeting problem?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Before running any signal check, confirm that the problem is the page rather than the targeting. The diagnostic is:"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-5 space-y-4","children":[["$","li","CTR on the ad itself",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-4 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"CTR on the ad itself"}],"$L2a"]}],"$L2b","$L2c","$L2d"]}]]}],"$L2e","$L2f","$L30","$L31","$L32","$L33"]}]}]
